r or TypeErrors.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:840:  tags: [tokenizer, autoprocessor, multimodal, apply_chat_template]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:841:  legacy_id: \"\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:842:- id: \"11.07\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:843:  phase: 11\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:844:  area: performance\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:846:  cause: Multi-pass LLM cycles (Critique, Open-Close, Arc Enhancer) force the model to stay active over multiple inference windows. On 4GB cards, the cumulative KV cache and model offloading overhead over 5+ passes causes extreme bus latency.\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:847:  fix: Implement an \"Optimization Profile\" (Obsidian/One-Shot) that defaults all iterative passes to OFF. One prompt, one script, zero offload cycles.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:848:  verify: 4GB script generation completes in a single window without the \"crawling\" effect found in multi-pass runs.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:849:  tags: [vram, 4gb, obsidian, performance, offloading]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:850:  legacy_id: \"\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:851:- id: \"11.08\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:852:  phase: 11\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:855:  cause: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:856:    Writer prompt addition required `TITLE: <name>` as first output line. Both streaming detector and post-stream parser match `NAME: text` shape as dialogue, and neither blacklist contained `TITLE`. Every title line got booked as character TITLE speaking the title text, polluting cast, eating word budget, nudging self-critique into deletion.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:857:  fix: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:858:    (1) Add `\"TITLE\"` to `_DIALOGUE_FALSE_POSITIVES` frozenset (line ~1545).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:859:    (2) Add `\"TITLE\"` to streaming heartbeat's inline false-positive tuple (line ~1885).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:860:    (3) Before `_parse_script`, extract `TITLE:` line via `_extract_title_from_script_text`, strip all `TITLE:` lines from script_text with regex, inject extracted value into title-resolution block. Log `TITLE_STRIP | extracted=...`.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:861:  verify: Next run shows `TITLE_STRIP | extracted='...'` AND ScriptWriter DONE's Characters list does NOT contain `TITLE`. Filename still varies. `TITLE_TRACE source=llm` still resolves correctly.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:867:  area: llm\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:868:  symptom: BatchBark finds 0 dialogue lines despite Grammarian reporting 20+. Bark bus renders only ANNOUNCER with no character dialogue. Silent 20-line drop between parser and BatchBark.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:869:  cause: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:870:    Three compounding gaps in FORMAT_NORM / parser chain for Mistral's bare `NAME: text` dialogue style:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:871:    (1) FORMAT_NORM skip heuristic treated `canonical_count >= 5` raw `NAME:` matches as already canonical; skipped LLM rewrite. But `_parse_script` had no pattern for bare `NAME: text` (only bracket tags).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:872:    (2) `_parse_script` bare `NAME:` lines hit \"treat as direction\" fallback and were lost.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:873:    (3) Permissive 2B-fallback only fired if dialogue_count == 0; one stray malformed tag short-circuited recovery of 20+ legitimate lines.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:879:  verify: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:880:    Next run shows `DIALOGUE_TRACK: 07_AFTER_PARSE | count=N` matching streaming count. `[BatchBark] Found N dialogue lines` shows N >= 15 for normal run (was 0 before). MP4 audio contains character dialogue.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:881:  tags: [format-norm, parser, bare-dialogue, mistral, skip-heuristic, fallback]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:882:  legacy_id: BUG-LOCAL-038\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:883:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:884:- id: \"11.10\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:885:  phase: 11\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:941:    9. Workflow JSON internal consistency\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:942:    10. Commit and push (Start-Job/batch on Windows)\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:943:    11. Verify push landed on remote\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:944:    12. Restart ComfyUI fully and run end-to-end\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:945:    13. Statistical RNG harness if RNG-adjacent\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:946:    14. GitHub HEAD lockstep verification\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:947:    15. Scan for 0-byte/BOM/missing registrations on remote\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:975:  fix: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:976:    Golden rule, if a senior pair-programmer would just do it, the AI should just do it. Install packages, fix errors, sync files, run regression, commit, push, batch related changes, report summary at end. Only escalate when a decision is required or a wall is hit (auth prompts, etc.).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:977:  verify: Number of \"please run this\" handoffs trends toward zero.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:978:  tags: [autonomy, ux, workflow]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:979:  legacy_id: \"16\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:980:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:981:- id: \"12.05\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:983:  area: pipeline-sync\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:984:  symptom: Same parameter has different defaults at parser/prompt/renderer layers.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:985:  cause: Multi-layer pipeline; one layer updated, others not.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:986:  fix: Grep for the value across the whole codebase before changing it. Add a hard cap at the rendering layer as a safety net (`min(value, MAX)`).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:987:  verify: All layers report same value.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:988:  tags: [pipeline, sync, multi-layer]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:989:  legacy_id: \"58\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1024:  symptom: git command hangs forever in PowerShell.\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1025:  cause: Windows Credential Manager opens GUI prompt AI cannot interact with. Or Git LFS filter (process=git-lfs filter-process) hangs every git op even on non-LFS repos. Or Windows Defender locks git.exe child processes.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1026:  fix: Wrap git in Start-Job with timeout. Remove [filter \"lfs\"] block from ~/.gitconfig. Add-MpPreference -ExclusionPath \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\" from admin terminal.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1027:  verify: git --version returns instantly.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1028:  tags: [git, powershell, lfs, defender, hang]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1029:  legacy_id: \"9.1\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1030:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1168:    Long generation runs produce scripts with garbled, duplicated, or out-of-place\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1169:    text blocks that look like error messages or partial prompts bleeding into the\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1170:    narrative. Downstream parsers and assemblers choke on the corruption.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1171:  cause: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1172:    A timeout wrapper around an LLM pass (e.g. critique-revision, arc-enhancer-echo)\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1173:    returns its fallback text directly concatenated into the same string stream as\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1174:    the real model output. When the main script body is built by joining strings,\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1507:  cause: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1508:    The input prompt is far larger than the model's configured context window.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1509:    NeMo 12B (and similar 128k-native models) have max_position_embeddings\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1510:    constrained at load time (e.g. to 2048 tokens) to limit KV cache VRAM.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1511:    However, transformers does NOT enforce this at the input level - it still\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1512:    accepts a 10,000-token prompt and pre-fills the FULL unrestricted KV cache,\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1513:    causing a massive VRAM spike and a proportionally long pre-fill stall before\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1514:    any tokens are generated. This is silent: no error, no warning, just a hang.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1515:  fix: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1516:    After tokenizing the prompt, check input length and truncate explicitly\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1517:    before calling model.generate():\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1518:      _context_cap = _LLM_CACHE.get(\"context_cap\", 8192)\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1519:      _max_input_tokens = max(64, _context_cap - max_new_tokens)\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1520:      _input_len = inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[-1]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1521:      if _input_len > _max_input_tokens:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1525:              inputs[\"attention_mask\"] = inputs[\"attention_mask\"][:, _trunc:]\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1526:          log.info(\"Prompt truncated: %d -> %d tokens\", _input_len, _max_input_tokens)\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1527:    Also add a 1-token warmup generate() call right after model load to front-load\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1528:    SDPA/BitsAndBytes CUDA kernel JIT compilation, eliminating a secondary cold-start\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1529:    stall on the very first real generate() call.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1530:  verify: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1531:    Runtime log shows \"PROMPT_GUARD: Truncated N -> M tokens\" on the first pass.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1532:    Token throughput immediately hits 13+ tok/s (no pre-fill stall).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1533:    Peak VRAM stays within the sovereignty buffer (e.g. < 9 GB for NeMo 12B 4-bit).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1534:    VRAM_CEILING_EXCEEDED no longer appears in logs.\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1535:  tags: [vram, llm, prompt-length, context-cap, prefill, stall, nemo, bitsandbytes, warmup, xphase-11]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1536:  legacy_id: \"\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1537:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1538:- id: \"12.34\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1539:  phase: 12\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1540:  area: git\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1705:  symptom: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1706:    POST /prompt returns HTTP 400 because widget values arrive in\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1707:    the wrong slots: numeric values land in string params, dropdown\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1708:    values land in the wrong dropdown, etc. Workflow renders fine in\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1709:    the UI but breaks on programmatic invocation.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1710:  cause: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1711:    Workflow\u001aAPI converters that walk widgets_values positionally\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1723:    Programmatic submission of the workflow JSON via\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1724:    /prompt returns HTTP 200 with no value_not_in_list /\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1725:    invalid_input_type errors, and the realized inputs match what\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1726:    the UI shows.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1727:  tags: [widget-drift, workflow-to-api, linked-inputs, positional]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1728:  legacy_id: BUG-LOCAL-003\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1729:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1733:  symptom: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1734:    POST /prompt rejects a dropdown value with\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1735:    `value_not_in_list: '[icon] standard (12 min)' not in\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1736:    ['[EMOJI] standard (12 min)', ...]`. The workflow JSON saved a\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1737:    real Unicode glyph (U+1F4FB radio etc.) in the slot but the\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1738:    INPUT_TYPES choice list uses a plain `[EMOJI]` text placeholder\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1739:    (or vice versa).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1753:    Round-trip a workflow JSON containing each dropdown form\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1754:    through the API; both the UI and /prompt accept it.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1755:  tags: [combo, encoding, emoji, api, exact-string-match]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1756:  legacy_id: BUG-LOCAL-005\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1757:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1758:- id: \"04.09\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1759:  phase: 4\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1811:    Capture a debug dump of both the `/object_info` schema for the\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1812:    node and the realized widget keys in the API prompt; their\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1813:    intersection should match every widgets_values slot.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1814:  tags: [widget-drift, object-info, input_types, schema-order]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1815:  legacy_id: BUG-LOCAL-008\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1816:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1817:- id: \"04.11\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1987:    target (e.g. user picks 8-minute target, output is 3.7\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1988:    minutes). The LLM prompt cites the same minute target but\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1989:    output is much shorter. Estimator was right by line count,\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1990:    wrong by duration.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1991:  cause: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1992:    User-facing units (minutes) are not measurable by the LLM -\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1993:    the LLM has no reliable internal mapping from words to\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1994:    spoken duration. Prompts that demand \"an N-minute episode\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1995:    rely on the model's vibe of length, which varies wildly by\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1996:    model and temperature. The downstream estimator typically\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1997:    uses a generic words-per-minute constant (e.g. 130 wpm for\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1998:    \"speech\") that does not match the actual TTS engine's pace\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:1999:    (e.g. Bark plays at ~67 wpm).\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2004:    to LLM-facing word count (`target_words = target_minutes *\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2005:    TTS_WPM`) in the prompt - \"write at least N words of\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2006:    dialogue\" is countable; \"write an N-minute episode\" is not.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2007:    Add a post-generation enforcement step that re-runs the LLM\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2008:    if word count is < 70% of target.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2009:  verify: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2010:    Across N=10 runs at the same target, observed runtime falls\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2266:    output directly - happiest path; (2) if parse fails, build a\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2267:    strict-JSON repair prompt that includes the failed raw output\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2268:    and the expected schema, call the LLM with very low\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2269:    temperature (0.05-0.15) and a smaller \"cleanup\" model when\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2270:    available, parse the repair output through the same\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2271:    extractor; (3) only if BOTH parses fail, fall back to a\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2272:    minimum-viable plan. Save raw output to a debug file every\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2465:    starter. A non-face reference has nothing to lock onto;\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2466:    the model falls back to text-prompt-driven face generation.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2467:  fix: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2468:    Class lesson: don't conflate conditioning-code shape with\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2469:    model capability. When a parameter exists in the upstream\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2470:    node API, READ THE NODE SOURCE to confirm what the parameter\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2471:    actually does. Specific case: when an audio-to-video model is\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2516:    Bookend / template enforcer regex doesn't match the modern\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2517:    prompt format. A required template section is detected as\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2518:    missing on every run. Secondary fallback fires repeatedly\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2519:    even when the original output is correct.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2520:  cause: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2521:    Regex format drift. The detection regex was written when the\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2522:    prompt asked for one format (e.g. bare `ANNOUNCER:`); the\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2523:    prompt was updated to a different format (e.g. bracketed\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2524:    `[VOICE: ANNOUNCER]`) but the regex was not updated. The\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2525:    primary detector never matches the new shape. Compounding:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2526:    the secondary fallback has no ultimate fallback - when it\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2527:    also fails, output ships in the bad shape.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2528:  fix: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2529:    Treat prompt format and detection regex as a paired contract.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2530:    When you change one, update the other in the same atomic\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2531:    commit. Detection regex should accept BOTH old and new\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2532:    formats during transitions:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2533:    `^(?:ANNOUNCER\\s*:|\\[VOICE\\s*:\\s*ANNOUNCER\\b)` with\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2534:    `IGNORECASE`. Widen the head/tail sniff window from 500 to\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2544:    shows ANNOUNCER role on first AND last line.\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2545:  tags: [llm, regex-format-drift, prompt-detector-contract, ultimate-fallback]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2546:  legacy_id: BUG-LOCAL-131\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2547:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2548:- id: \"11.23\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2549:  phase: 11\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2550:  area: llm\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2551:  symptom: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2552:    Length prompts ask for \"AT LEAST N words\" of a small target\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2553:    (e.g. 30 words for a smoke run). The LLM produces 200+ words.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2554:    Floor satisfied; ceiling absent; downstream rendering takes\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2555:    hours instead of minutes.\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2556:  cause: |\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2557:    \"AT LEAST N words\" is a floor with no upper bound. The LLM\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2573:    word count is between 25 and 45.\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2574:  tags: [llm, length-prompt, floor-ceiling, smoke-preset, overshoot]\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2575:  legacy_id: BUG-LOCAL-132\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2576:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2577:- id: \"12.39\"\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2578:  phase: 12\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2579:  area: llm-routing\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2681:  cause: |\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2682:    Prompt audit reveals three gaps: (1) the min-line floor is\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2683:    asserted in only 1 of N prompts (system prompt), so user\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2684:    prompts and follow-up passes don't re-assert it - LLMs\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2685:    under-weight system-prompt rules vs user-prompt rules on\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2686:    short calls; (2) ZERO prompts explicitly forbid narration-\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2687:    only output; the failure mode is unnamed in the prompt set;\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2688:    (3) prompts insist on ONE specific format (e.g. `[VOICE:\r\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2689:    NAME, ...]`) when the underlying model often emits a\r\n> C:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\comfyui-custom-node-survival-guide\\BUG_BIBLE.yaml:2690:    parseable shorthand variant naturally - the pr