posed 474 characters.\r\n    A SECOND defect hid behind the first and is the mechanical half: the\r\n    trimmer dropped whole COMMA-SEPARATED phrases, and the config surfaces\r\n    are long comma-FREE prose. On those the trimmer is a NO-OP -- it finds\r\n    one phrase, cannot drop it, and returns the text at its original length.\r\n    A trimmer that cannot shrink its most likely input is not a trimmer.\r\n  fix: |\r\n    Parameterise the budget tests over the OPTION-ABSENT path explicitly,\r\n    and over every shipped config value rather than one convenient default:\r\n    role x pack x register key, with the optional input withheld. A fixture\r\n    that always supplies an optional input is testing the caller, not the\r\n    default. State the arithmetic in the test's own failure message (which\r\n    surface contributed how many characters) so the next failure names its\r\n    cause instead of only its total.\r\n    For the trimmer: make it fall back from phrase boundaries to WORD\r\n    boundaries so it can shrink comma-free prose, and never let a cut end on\r\n- artifact: `signal_lost_reel_of_mystery_20260815_041350` (media_archive),\r\n  `signal_lost_midnights_ticktock_20260815_045020` (public_domain),\r\n  `signal_lost_ghost_of_elsinore_20260815_050626` (shakespeare). Overnight\r\n  six-bank gate, 2026-08-15.\r\n- symptom: operator on the archive episode -- *\"What news story???\"*. The\r\n  closing announcer said only *\"Clarisse's gaze meets the reel's enigmatic\r\n  label\"*.\r\n- what actually happened: `meta.ledger_clean.rows[b016].before` holds the\r\n  COMPOSED row -- an authored bridge, `\": \"`, then the factual close *\"In other\r\n  news, the Library of Congress announces its film loans for the month,\r\n  including 'None But the Lonely Heart', 'Symphony of Swing', and 'The Man With\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
